(479, 11, 1, '<br>The Sunrise Hotel<br>The Sunrise Hotel is a three-star hotel near the city center. It has 80 guest rooms: 40 standard rooms, 25 deluxe rooms, and 15 family rooms. The hotel provides a restaurant, a swimming pool, a fitness center, and a meeting room. <br>The restaurant serves breakfast from 6:00 to 10:00 a.m. The swimming pool opens at 7:00 a.m. and closes at 9:00 p.m. The fitness center is open from 6:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m. Free Wi-Fi is available in all rooms and public areas. <br> What is the main purpose of the text?', 1, ' To explain how to book a hotel room ', ' To describe the facilities and features of a hotel ', ' To tell a story about a hotel guest ', ' To persuade people to become hotel employees ', ' To explain how to operate a swimming pool', 'B', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(480, 11, 2, '<br>The Sunrise Hotel<br>The Sunrise Hotel is a three-star hotel near the city center. It has 80 guest rooms: 40 standard rooms, 25 deluxe rooms, and 15 family rooms. The hotel provides a restaurant, a swimming pool, a fitness center, and a meeting room. <br>The restaurant serves breakfast from 6:00 to 10:00 a.m. The swimming pool opens at 7:00 a.m. and closes at 9:00 p.m. The fitness center is open from 6:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m. Free Wi-Fi is available in all rooms and public areas. <br> How many guest rooms does the Sunrise Hotel have?', 1, ' Forty rooms ', ' Sixty-five rooms ', ' Seventy rooms ', ' Eighty rooms ', ' Eighty-five rooms', 'D', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(481, 11, 3, '<br>The Sunrise Hotel<br>The Sunrise Hotel is a three-star hotel near the city center. It has 80 guest rooms: 40 standard rooms, 25 deluxe rooms, and 15 family rooms. The hotel provides a restaurant, a swimming pool, a fitness center, and a meeting room. <br>The restaurant serves breakfast from 6:00 to 10:00 a.m. The swimming pool opens at 7:00 a.m. and closes at 9:00 p.m. The fitness center is open from 6:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m. Free Wi-Fi is available in all rooms and public areas. <br> What percentage of the hotel&#39;s rooms are deluxe rooms?', 1, ' 18.75% ', ' 25%', ' 31.25% ', ' 40% ', ' 50%', 'B', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(482, 11, 4, ' <br>The Sunrise Hotel<br>The Sunrise Hotel is a three-star hotel near the city center. It has 80 guest rooms: 40 standard rooms, 25 deluxe rooms, and 15 family rooms. The hotel provides a restaurant, a swimming pool, a fitness center, and a meeting room. <br>The restaurant serves breakfast from 6:00 to 10:00 a.m. The swimming pool opens at 7:00 a.m. and closes at 9:00 p.m. The fitness center is open from 6:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m. Free Wi-Fi is available in all rooms and public areas. <br>A guest wants to swim at 8:30 p.m. Is the swimming pool still open?', 1, ' No, it closes at 8:00 p.m. ', ' No, it closes at 7:00 p.m. ', ' Yes, it closes at 9:00 p.m. ', ' Yes, it closes at 10:00 p.m. ', ' No, it closes at 6:00 p.m.', 'C', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(483, 11, 5, '<br>The Sunrise Hotel<br>The Sunrise Hotel is a three-star hotel near the city center. It has 80 guest rooms: 40 standard rooms, 25 deluxe rooms, and 15 family rooms. The hotel provides a restaurant, a swimming pool, a fitness center, and a meeting room. <br>The restaurant serves breakfast from 6:00 to 10:00 a.m. The swimming pool opens at 7:00 a.m. and closes at 9:00 p.m. The fitness center is open from 6:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m. Free Wi-Fi is available in all rooms and public areas. <br> Why is the hotel suitable for business travelers?', 1, ' It offers the cheapest rooms in the city. ', ' It is located near the beach. ', ' It provides free meals all day. ', ' It has the largest swimming pool. ', ' It is near the business district and has meeting facilities.', 'E', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(484, 11, 6, '<br>The Lost Wallet<br>One afternoon, Rina was walking home from school when she found a wallet near a bus stop. Inside it, she found an identity card and Rp500,000. She thought about keeping the money because her schoolbag was broken and she needed a new one. <br>However, Rina remembered her teacher&#39;s advice that honesty was more valuable than money. She used the address on the identity card to find the owner, Mr. Budi, who lived nearby. <br>When Rina returned the wallet, Mr. Budi was relieved because the money was intended to pay his electricity bill. He offered Rina a reward, but she politely refused. Instead, he thanked her and offered to help repair her schoolbag. <br> What is the main problem in the story?', 1, ' Rina lost her schoolbag. ', ' Mr. Budi could not pay his electricity bill. ', ' Rina had to choose between keeping and returning the wallet. ', ' Rina could not find her school. ', ' Mr. Budi refused to help Rina.', 'C', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(485, 11, 7, '<br>The Lost Wallet<br>One afternoon, Rina was walking home from school when she found a wallet near a bus stop. Inside it, she found an identity card and Rp500,000. She thought about keeping the money because her schoolbag was broken and she needed a new one. <br>However, Rina remembered her teacher&#39;s advice that honesty was more valuable than money. She used the address on the identity card to find the owner, Mr. Budi, who lived nearby. <br>When Rina returned the wallet, Mr. Budi was relieved because the money was intended to pay his electricity bill. He offered Rina a reward, but she politely refused. Instead, he thanked her and offered to help repair her schoolbag. <br> Why did Rina initially consider keeping the money?', 1, ' She wanted to buy a new schoolbag. ', ' She wanted to pay Mr. Budi&#39;s bill.', ' She wanted to give it to her teacher. ', ' She had lost her own wallet. ', ' She wanted to buy an identity card.', 'A', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(486, 11, 8, '<br>The Lost Wallet<br>One afternoon, Rina was walking home from school when she found a wallet near a bus stop. Inside it, she found an identity card and Rp500,000. She thought about keeping the money because her schoolbag was broken and she needed a new one. <br>However, Rina remembered her teacher&#39;s advice that honesty was more valuable than money. She used the address on the identity card to find the owner, Mr. Budi, who lived nearby. <br>When Rina returned the wallet, Mr. Budi was relieved because the money was intended to pay his electricity bill. He offered Rina a reward, but she politely refused. Instead, he thanked her and offered to help repair her schoolbag. <br> What lesson can be learned from the story?', 1, ' Money is more important than friendship. ', ' People should avoid helping strangers. ', ' Rewards are necessary for every good action. ', ' Honesty and kindness are valuable qualities. ', ' Students should never take the bus.', 'D', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(487, 11, 9, '<br>The Lost Wallet<br>One afternoon, Rina was walking home from school when she found a wallet near a bus stop. Inside it, she found an identity card and Rp500,000. She thought about keeping the money because her schoolbag was broken and she needed a new one. <br>However, Rina remembered her teacher&#39;s advice that honesty was more valuable than money. She used the address on the identity card to find the owner, Mr. Budi, who lived nearby. <br>When Rina returned the wallet, Mr. Budi was relieved because the money was intended to pay his electricity bill. He offered Rina a reward, but she politely refused. Instead, he thanked her and offered to help repair her schoolbag. <br> If Rina had kept Rp500,000, how much money would Mr. Budi have lost?', 1, ' Rp50,000 ', ' Rp100,000 ', ' Rp250,000 ', ' Rp400,000 ', ' Rp500,000', 'E', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(488, 11, 10, '<br>The Lost Wallet<br>One afternoon, Rina was walking home from school when she found a wallet near a bus stop. Inside it, she found an identity card and Rp500,000. She thought about keeping the money because her schoolbag was broken and she needed a new one. <br>However, Rina remembered her teacher&#39;s advice that honesty was more valuable than money. She used the address on the identity card to find the owner, Mr. Budi, who lived nearby. <br>When Rina returned the wallet, Mr. Budi was relieved because the money was intended to pay his electricity bill. He offered Rina a reward, but she politely refused. Instead, he thanked her and offered to help repair her schoolbag. <br> The word &ldquo;relieved&rdquo; in the text is closest in meaning to ....', 1, ' Angry ', ' Worried ', ' Feeling less worried ', ' Disappointed ', ' Confused', 'C', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(489, 11, 11, '<br>An Internship Experience at a Hotel<br>Last month, Dimas, a hospitality student, completed a five-day internship at Grand Palace Hotel. On the first day, he learned how to welcome guests and answer telephone calls. On the second and third days, he assisted the housekeeping team in preparing guest rooms. <br>On the fourth day, Dimas helped the receptionist check guests in and out under supervision. On the final day, his supervisor evaluated his performance. Dimas received 85 points for communication skills and 90 points for discipline. <br>What is the text mainly about?', 1, ' Dimas&#39;s holiday at a luxury hotel ', ' Dimas&#39;s internship experience at a hotel ', ' The history of Grand Palace Hotel ', ' The process of building a hotel ', ' The responsibilities of a hotel manager', 'B', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(490, 11, 12, '<br>An Internship Experience at a Hotel<br>Last month, Dimas, a hospitality student, completed a five-day internship at Grand Palace Hotel. On the first day, he learned how to welcome guests and answer telephone calls. On the second and third days, he assisted the housekeeping team in preparing guest rooms. <br>On the fourth day, Dimas helped the receptionist check guests in and out under supervision. On the final day, his supervisor evaluated his performance. Dimas received 85 points for communication skills and 90 points for discipline. <br> On which days did Dimas work with the housekeeping team?', 1, ' The first and second days ', ' The second and third days ', ' The third and fourth days ', ' The fourth and fifth days ', ' The first and fifth days', 'B', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
