(513, 11, 35, '<br> Blue Ocean Hotel Room Rates<br>Blue Ocean Hotel offers three types of rooms. A standard room costs Rp400,000 per night and accommodates two guests. A deluxe room costs Rp600,000 per night and accommodates two guests. A family room costs Rp900,000 per night and accommodates four guests. <br>All rooms include air conditioning, Wi-Fi, and breakfast. Guests who stay for three consecutive nights receive a 10% discount on the total room cost. <br>A family of four stays for two nights in a family room. How much must they pay before any discount?', 1, ' Rp900,000 ', ' Rp1,200,000 ', ' Rp1,500,000 ', ' Rp1,600,000 ', ' Rp1,800,000', 'E', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(514, 11, 36, '<br>A School Visit to a Local Hotel<br>Last Friday, 36 students and three teachers visited a local hotel to learn about hospitality operations. They arrived at 8:00 a.m. and were welcomed by the hotel training manager. <br>First, the students attended a presentation about front office duties. Next, they visited the housekeeping department and learned how staff prepared rooms for arriving guests. After lunch, they observed the restaurant team arranging tables and serving customers. <br>The visit ended at 2:00 p.m. The students returned to school with a better understanding of hotel operations. <br> What was the purpose of the school visit?', 1, ' To celebrate the hotel&#39;s anniversary ', ' To apply for hotel management positions ', ' To learn about hospitality operations ', ' To organize a school competition ', ' To inspect the hotel&#39;s financial records', 'C', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(515, 11, 37, '<br>A School Visit to a Local Hotel<br>Last Friday, 36 students and three teachers visited a local hotel to learn about hospitality operations. They arrived at 8:00 a.m. and were welcomed by the hotel training manager. <br>First, the students attended a presentation about front office duties. Next, they visited the housekeeping department and learned how staff prepared rooms for arriving guests. After lunch, they observed the restaurant team arranging tables and serving customers. <br>The visit ended at 2:00 p.m. The students returned to school with a better understanding of hotel operations. <br> How many people were in the visiting group?', 1, ' 33 ', ' 36 ', ' 37 ', ' 39 ', ' 42', 'D', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
