(517, 11, 39, '<br>A School Visit to a Local Hotel<br>Last Friday, 36 students and three teachers visited a local hotel to learn about hospitality operations. They arrived at 8:00 a.m. and were welcomed by the hotel training manager. <br>First, the students attended a presentation about front office duties. Next, they visited the housekeeping department and learned how staff prepared rooms for arriving guests. After lunch, they observed the restaurant team arranging tables and serving customers. <br>The visit ended at 2:00 p.m. The students returned to school with a better understanding of hotel operations. <br> Which department did the students visit after the front office presentation?', 1, ' Housekeeping ', ' Security ', ' Accounting ', ' Engineering ', ' Human resources', 'A', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(518, 11, 40, '<br>A School Visit to a Local Hotel<br>Last Friday, 36 students and three teachers visited a local hotel to learn about hospitality operations. They arrived at 8:00 a.m. and were welcomed by the hotel training manager. <br>First, the students attended a presentation about front office duties. Next, they visited the housekeeping department and learned how staff prepared rooms for arriving guests. After lunch, they observed the restaurant team arranging tables and serving customers. <br>The visit ended at 2:00 p.m. The students returned to school with a better understanding of hotel operations. <br> The phrase &ldquo;a better understanding of hotel operations&rdquo; means that the students ....', 1, ' could replace their teachers with hotel employees ', ' understood hotel work more clearly ', ' avoided learning theory at school ', ' managed the entire hotel independently ', ' shortened their school timetable permanently', 'B', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(519, 11, 41, '<br>How to Calculate a Hotel Guest&#39;s Bill<br>A receptionist must calculate a guest&#39;s bill accurately before checkout. <br>1.Confirm the room type and the number of nights. <br>2.Multiply the room rate by the number of nights. <br>3.Add additional charges, such as laundry or restaurant expenses. <br>4.Subtract applicable discounts. <br>5.Check the final amount and explain the bill to the guest. <br>For example, a guest stays in a deluxe room costing Rp600,000 per night for two nights. The guest spends Rp150,000 on laundry and receives a 5% discount on the room cost only. <br>The room cost is Rp1,200,000. The discount is Rp60,000. The final bill is Rp1,290,000. <br> What is the purpose of the procedure?', 1, ' To describe different hotel departments ', ' To explain how to calculate a hotel guest&#39;s bill ', ' To persuade guests to use laundry services ', ' To tell a story about a receptionist ', ' To explain how to decorate a hotel room', 'B', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(520, 11, 42, '<br>How to Calculate a Hotel Guest&#39;s Bill<br>A receptionist must calculate a guest&#39;s bill accurately before checkout. <br>1.Confirm the room type and the number of nights. <br>2.Multiply the room rate by the number of nights. <br>3.Add additional charges, such as laundry or restaurant expenses. <br>4.Subtract applicable discounts. <br>5.Check the final amount and explain the bill to the guest. <br>For example, a guest stays in a deluxe room costing Rp600,000 per night for two nights. The guest spends Rp150,000 on laundry and receives a 5% discount on the room cost only. <br>The room cost is Rp1,200,000. The discount is Rp60,000. The final bill is Rp1,290,000. <br> How much is the room cost before the discount?', 1, ' Rp600,000 ', ' Rp900,000 ', ' Rp1,000,000 ', ' Rp1,100,000 ', ' Rp1,200,000', 'E', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
