(524, 11, 46, '<br>The Importance of Reading for Vocational Students<br>Reading should become a regular habit for vocational students. Some students believe that practical skills alone are enough to prepare them for work. However, reading also plays an important role in developing professional competence. <br>First, reading helps students understand instructions, workplace regulations, and technical information. Hotel employees, for example, need to read reservation details carefully to avoid booking errors. Second, reading improves vocabulary and communication. Third, reading develops critical thinking because readers must identify main ideas, compare information, and evaluate arguments. <br>Schools can encourage reading by providing accessible materials and setting aside time for independent reading. A consistent habit of 20 minutes a day can provide regular practice. <br> What is the writer&#39;s main point?', 1, ' Practical training should be removed from vocational schools. ', ' Students should read only English books. ', ' Reading should be a regular part of vocational education. ', ' Students must read for several hours every day. ', ' Technical information is unnecessary for hotel workers.', 'C', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(525, 11, 47, ' <br>The Importance of Reading for Vocational Students<br>Reading should become a regular habit for vocational students. Some students believe that practical skills alone are enough to prepare them for work. However, reading also plays an important role in developing professional competence. <br>First, reading helps students understand instructions, workplace regulations, and technical information. Hotel employees, for example, need to read reservation details carefully to avoid booking errors. Second, reading improves vocabulary and communication. Third, reading develops critical thinking because readers must identify main ideas, compare information, and evaluate arguments. <br>Schools can encourage reading by providing accessible materials and setting aside time for independent reading. A consistent habit of 20 minutes a day can provide regular practice. <br>According to the text, how can reading help hotel employees?', 1, ' It eliminates the need to communicate with guests. ', ' It helps them understand reservation details accurately. ', ' It allows them to ignore workplace regulations. ', ' It guarantees promotion to management positions. ', ' It replaces the need for practical training.', 'B', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
