(574, 13, 1, '<br>Read the dialogue below carefully!<br>Rina: Did you see the video about the flood that everyone is sharing? <br>Dani: Yes, but I&#39;m not sure it&#39;s true. The video looks old. <br>Rina: In my opinion, we should check the source before sharing it. <br>Dani: I couldn&#39;t agree more. Spreading hoaxes can make people panic. <br> What are Rina and Dani mainly talking about?', 1, 'A flood that happened in their town', 'A new video-editing application', 'Checking information before sharing it online', 'Their plan to go to the beach', 'Their homework about floods', 'C', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(575, 13, 2, '<br>Read the dialogue below carefully! <br>Rina: Did you see the video about the flood that everyone is sharing? <br>Dani: Yes, but I&#39;m not sure it&#39;s true. The video looks old. <br>Rina: In my opinion, we should check the source before sharing it. <br>Dani: I couldn&#39;t agree more. Spreading hoaxes can make people panic. <br>  In the dialogue, &#39;I couldn&#39;t agree more&#39; means that Dani ____.', 1, 'Disagrees with Rina', 'Strongly agrees with Rina', 'Is confused by Rina', 'Wants to change the topic', 'Asks Rina for help', 'B', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(576, 13, 3, '<br>Read the dialogue below carefully! <br>Rina: Did you see the video about the flood that everyone is sharing? <br>Dani: Yes, but I&#39;m not sure it&#39;s true. The video looks old. <br>Rina: In my opinion, we should check the source before sharing it. <br>Dani: I couldn&#39;t agree more. Spreading hoaxes can make people panic. <br>  Which expression is used to state an opinion in the dialogue?', 1, 'Did you see the video', 'I&#39;m not sure it&#39;s true', 'The video looks old', 'In my opinion', 'Spreading hoaxes', 'D', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(577, 13, 4, '<br>Social media has become a part of our daily life. We use it to chat with friends, share photos, and find information. However, not every post on social media is true or safe. Some people spread hoaxes, and others write hurtful comments. To use social media wisely, we should protect our personal data, think before we post, and respect other users. We should also limit our screen time so that we still have time to study, sleep, and talk to our families. Therefore, let&#39;s become smart and responsible users. <br>  What is the main idea of the text?', 1, 'Social media is dangerous for everyone.', 'Teenagers should stop using social media.', 'Hoaxes are the most common posts online.', 'Social media helps people earn money.', 'People need to use social media wisely and responsibly.', 'E', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(578, 13, 5, '<br>Social media has become a part of our daily life. We use it to chat with friends, share photos, and find information. However, not every post on social media is true or safe. Some people spread hoaxes, and others write hurtful comments. To use social media wisely, we should protect our personal data, think before we post, and respect other users. We should also limit our screen time so that we still have time to study, sleep, and talk to our families. Therefore, let&#39;s become smart and responsible users. <br>   What is the author&#39;s main purpose in writing the text?', 1, 'To persuade readers to use social media wisely', 'To entertain readers with a funny story', 'To describe a social media application', 'To explain how social media was invented', 'To advertise a new phone', 'A', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(579, 13, 6, '<br>Social media has become a part of our daily life. We use it to chat with friends, share photos, and find information. However, not every post on social media is true or safe. Some people spread hoaxes, and others write hurtful comments. To use social media wisely, we should protect our personal data, think before we post, and respect other users. We should also limit our screen time so that we still have time to study, sleep, and talk to our families. Therefore, let&#39;s become smart and responsible users. <br> &#39;Not every post on social media is true or safe.&#39; We can infer that users should ____.', 1, 'Believe every post they read', 'Check information before trusting or sharing it', 'Delete their social media accounts', 'Only follow famous people', 'Post more photos', 'B', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(580, 13, 7, '<br>Social media has become a part of our daily life. We use it to chat with friends, share photos, and find information. However, not every post on social media is true or safe. Some people spread hoaxes, and others write hurtful comments. To use social media wisely, we should protect our personal data, think before we post, and respect other users. We should also limit our screen time so that we still have time to study, sleep, and talk to our families. Therefore, let&#39;s become smart and responsible users. <br> Which is NOT mentioned as a way to use social media wisely?', 1, 'Protecting personal data', 'Thinking before posting', 'Respecting other users', 'Following as many accounts as possible', 'Limiting screen time', 'D', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(581, 13, 8, '<br>Read the dialogue below carefully! <br>Mother: Nadia, why did you put the banana peels in the plastic bin? <br>Nadia: Oh, sorry, Mom. I thought all trash goes into one bin. <br>Mother: Not really. Organic waste like peels goes into the green bin, and plastic goes into the yellow one. <br>Nadia: I see. I&#39;ll separate them from now on. <br> Where should Nadia put the banana peels?', 1, 'In the green bin', 'In the yellow bin', 'In the blue bin', 'Outside the house', 'In the plastic bag', 'A', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(582, 13, 9, '<br>Read the dialogue below carefully! <br>Mother: Nadia, why did you put the banana peels in the plastic bin? <br>Nadia: Oh, sorry, Mom. I thought all trash goes into one bin. <br>Mother: Not really. Organic waste like peels goes into the green bin, and plastic goes into the yellow one. <br>Nadia: I see. I&#39;ll separate them from now on. <br>  Which one is a subject question based on the dialogue?', 1, 'What did Nadia put in the plastic bin?', 'Where did Nadia put the banana peels?', 'Why did Mother ask Nadia?', 'When will Nadia separate the waste?', 'Who put the banana peels in the plastic bin?', 'E', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(583, 13, 10, '<br>Read the dialogue below carefully! <br>Mother: Nadia, why did you put the banana peels in the plastic bin? <br>Nadia: Oh, sorry, Mom. I thought all trash goes into one bin. <br>Mother: Not really. Organic waste like peels goes into the green bin, and plastic goes into the yellow one. <br>Nadia: I see. I&#39;ll separate them from now on. <br> What can be inferred about Nadia?', 1, 'She never helps with housework.', 'She dislikes the green bin.', 'She did not know how to separate waste before.', 'She refuses to follow her mother&#39;s advice.', 'She works as a waste collector.', 'C', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(584, 13, 11, '<br><b>My Grandmother&#39;s Kitchen</b><br>My grandmother&#39;s kitchen is the warmest place in our house. It is a small wooden room with a big old brown table in the middle. In the morning, the smell of fried rice and sweet tea fills the air. I can hear the sound of boiling water and my grandmother humming an old song. The tiles feel cool under my feet, and the first bite of her spicy sambal makes my tongue burn. Every time I enter the room, I feel safe and happy. <br>  What is the main idea of the text?', 1, 'The writer learns to cook fried rice.', 'The writer&#39;s house is small and old.', 'The writer&#39;s grandmother&#39;s kitchen is a warm and comfortable place.', 'The writer dislikes spicy food.', 'The writer&#39;s grandmother is a famous cook.', 'C', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(585, 13, 12, '<br><b>My Grandmother&#39;s Kitchen</b><br>My grandmother&#39;s kitchen is the warmest place in our house. It is a small wooden room with a big old brown table in the middle. In the morning, the smell of fried rice and sweet tea fills the air. I can hear the sound of boiling water and my grandmother humming an old song. The tiles feel cool under my feet, and the first bite of her spicy sambal makes my tongue burn. Every time I enter the room, I feel safe and happy. <br>   Which sense is described in &#39;the first bite of her spicy sambal makes my tongue burn&#39;?', 1, 'Taste', 'Smell', 'Hearing', 'Sight', 'Touch ', 'A', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(586, 13, 13, '<br><b>My Grandmother&#39;s Kitchen</b><br>My grandmother&#39;s kitchen is the warmest place in our house. It is a small wooden room with a big old brown table in the middle. In the morning, the smell of fried rice and sweet tea fills the air. I can hear the sound of boiling water and my grandmother humming an old song. The tiles feel cool under my feet, and the first bite of her spicy sambal makes my tongue burn. Every time I enter the room, I feel safe and happy. <br> Which phrase uses the correct order of adjectives?', 1, 'A wooden round beautiful table', 'A beautiful round wooden table', 'A round beautiful wooden table', 'A beautiful wooden round table', 'A wooden beautiful round table', 'B', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(587, 13, 14, '<br><b>My Grandmother&#39;s Kitchen</b><br>My grandmother&#39;s kitchen is the warmest place in our house. It is a small wooden room with a big old brown table in the middle. In the morning, the smell of fried rice and sweet tea fills the air. I can hear the sound of boiling water and my grandmother humming an old song. The tiles feel cool under my feet, and the first bite of her spicy sambal makes my tongue burn. Every time I enter the room, I feel safe and happy. <br> What is the author&#39;s purpose in writing the text?', 1, 'To persuade readers to cook at home', 'To inform readers how to make fried rice', 'To entertain readers with a funny story', 'To explain why kitchens are important', 'To describe the writer&#39;s grandmother&#39;s kitchen', 'E', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(588, 13, 15, '<br>Read the dialogue below carefully! <br>Bima:  I think students should be allowed to use their phones during lessons. <br>Mrs. Sari:  I&#39;m afraid I don&#39;t agree. Phones can distract you from the lesson. <br>Bima:  But we can use them to look for information, Ma&#39;am. <br>Mrs. Sari:  That&#39;s a good point, Bima. Let&#39;s use them only when I ask you to. <br> How does Mrs. Sari first respond to Bima&#39;s opinion?', 1, 'She agrees completely.', 'She ignores him.', 'She becomes angry.', 'She disagrees politely.', 'She thanks him.', 'D', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
